 # quoted-contact-import
 
 Small local library. Run `npm test`.
+
+`parseRows(text)` parses comma-separated records. LF and CRLF terminate records;
+one trailing terminator does not create an extra row. Fields retain whitespace,
+Unicode, and empty values, including a trailing empty field. A field beginning
+with `"` is quoted: commas and line breaks are allowed inside it, and `""`
+represents one quote. After its closing quote only a comma, record terminator,
+or end of input is valid. Quotes in unquoted fields, unclosed quotes, and bare
+CR characters are syntax errors. No trimming or backslash escaping is applied.
+
+`importContacts(text)` treats the first row as case-sensitive headers. Headers
+must be unique and include `name` and `email`; extra columns are ignored. Every
+data row must have the same width as the header row. Invalid headers or widths
+throw `TypeError`, while malformed CSV syntax throws `SyntaxError`.
diff --git a/src/contacts.mjs b/src/contacts.mjs
